&lt;p&gt;Elon Musk&amp;rsquo;s SpaceX has come under scrutiny over reported disruptions to Starlink satellite internet services used by Ukrainian forces, with President Volodymyr Zelenskyy accusing the company of restricting access during the war against Russia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A report by The Wall Street Journal, citing officials familiar with the matter, said Musk had directed an intentional slowdown of Ukraine&amp;rsquo;s military Starlink network. The reported move triggered concern in Kyiv and left the Donald Trump administration bewildered, according to the report.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;However, senior US officials have denied that Washington ordered any slowdown. Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth said the US military had not directed a reduction in satellite services, while Secretary of State Marco Rubio rejected claims that the White House was responsible for the reported disruption.&lt;/p&gt;
